<title>UK: Amersham buys Italian nuclear medicine firm.</title>
<headline>Amersham buys Italian nuclear medicine firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amersham International Plc said on Monday that it had bought the nuclear medicine business of Italy's Sorin Biomedica SpA for an initial 4.3 million stg.</p>
<p>Amersham said the acquisition would boost its position in southern Europe and Germany, and make it the market leader in nuclear medicine in Italy.  </p>
<p>Amersham said it would pay another 4.3 million stg for Sorin Diagnostics SpA before the end of June 1997, with further payments of between 5 billion lire and 28 billion lire payable over eight years depending on levels of sales.</p>
<p>The business will trade as Amersham Sorin Radiofarmaci.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
